alidation and performing all relevant ERC20 token transfers","methods":{"approveProof(bytes32)":{"details":"Approve a proofHash for spending a users deposited funds, this is one way and must be called by the owner of the funds","params":{"_proofHash":"- keccack256 hash of the inner proof public inputs"}},"depositPendingFunds(uint256,uint256,address)":{"details":"Deposit funds as part of the first stage of the two stage deposit. Non-permit flow","params":{"amount":"- number of tokens being deposited","assetId":"- unique ID of the asset","depositorAddress":"- address from which funds are being transferred to the contract"}},"depositPendingFundsPermit(uint256,uint256,address,address,uint256,uint256,uint8,bytes32,bytes32)":{"details":"Deposit funds as part of the first stage of the two stage deposit. Permit flow","params":{"amount":"- number of tokens being deposited","assetId":"- unique ID of the asset","deadline":"- when the permit signature expires","depositorAddress":"- address from which funds are being transferred to the contract","permitApprovalAmount":"- amount permit signature is approving","r":"- ECDSA sig param","s":"- ECDSA sig param","spender":"- address being granted approval to spend the funds","v":"- ECDSA sig param"}},"escapeHatch(bytes,bytes,bytes)":{"details":"Process a rollup - decode the rollup, update relevant state variables and verify the proof","params":{"proofData":"- cryptographic proof data associated with a rollup","signatures":"- bytes array of secp256k1 ECDSA signatures, authorising a transfer of tokens from the publicOwner for the particular inner proof in question. There is a signature for each inner proof. Structure of each signature in the bytes array is: 0x00 - 0x20 : r 0x20 - 0x40 : s 0x40 - 0x60 : v (in form: 0x0000....0001b for example)","viewingKeys":"- viewingKeys for the notes submitted in the rollup. Note: not used in the logic of the rollupProcessor contract, but called here as a convenient to place data on chain"}},"getAssetP